{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">An agent that calls the model once and executes blindly can only be as right as its first guess — it has no way to notice a wrong one.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Plan the next action, act on it for real, observe the actual result, and feed that observation back into the next plan — repeat until the model's own judgment says the goal is met.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Cap the iteration count, surface the loop's live state in the UI, and decide deliberately how much raw observation content stays in context — a loop that can replan also needs a way to stop and a way to be watched.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
